    {
      "id": "card.ancient_rome.050.c12",
      "type": "checkpoint",
      "headline": "Milestone: halfway to Mastery",
      "learned": [
        "How Augustus ruled alone but kept the Senate, consuls and elections, so Rome still looked like a republic.",
        "How Caesar's teenage heir used his famous name to beat the assassins, then Antony and Cleopatra at Actium.",
        "Why marble temples, the Aeneid and even the month of August all helped build Augustus's image.",
        "What the Pax Romana made possible inside the empire, and why fighting still went on at the frontiers."
      ]
    }
